  "policy_prompt_for_action": [
    {
      "modify_from": "For a resting cube, localize the center of its visible top face on its top-face plane, approximately z=0.04 m; the recovered x,y is its pickup center.",
      "modify_to": "For a resting cube, identify the center of the actual top face, excluding visible side faces, and intersect its calibrated camera ray with the top-face plane, approximately z=0.02 m for these cubes; the recovered x,y is its pickup center. Apply this to both initial pickup and regrasping on the target. Cross-check front and wrist estimates when both clearly show the top face; do not average projections of different physical features. This feature-localization height is distinct from the commanded grasp TCP height, which remains z=0.02 m."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "At cube_lifted, move closed to the target center at z=0.15 m before lowering. This alignment is needed even for repeated placements with only a few millimeters of displacement. If the target-hover waypoint differs from the current TCP position by less than 2 mm, omit that redundant motion and lower directly.",
      "modify_to": "At cube_lifted, always command a separate closed-gripper alignment at the target center and nominal z=0.15 m before lowering, including repeated placements already nearly centered over the target. Construct the center-corrected hover waypoint first. If its positional displacement from the current TCP is less than 2 mm, retain the target-center x,y and raise the waypoint z by 3–5 mm to satisfy the minimum displacement. Only after observing completion of this alignment recognize target_hover and apply descent-and-release. Allow ordinary small tracking errors and very short nonzero alignment motions when recognizing completion; do not skip alignment or recognize it merely because it was commanded."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Preserve the explicit rule for omitting a redundant target-hover motion at cube_lifted.",
      "modify_to": ""
    }
  ],
  "refused": "No substantive correction in this round's report is refused. The top-face height replaces Round 1's 0.04 m prescription because this round identifies it as the source of systematic pickup localization errors; the calibrated projection and independent-center rules remain intact. The target-hover omission and Round 1's preservation of that exception are removed because they bypass the required observed closed-gripper alignment. The minimum-displacement safeguard remains intact. No duplicate yaw rule, episode-specific coordinates, sub-2-mm waypoint exception, or memory changes are added."
}
